 ## Overview
-RLE4 Ray Tracing is a ray-marching and voxel-intersection algorithm that traverses an RLE4 (Run-Length Encoded 4D) compressed volume structure, also known as Map4, to locate the first occupied voxel along a ray or to colorize a voxel based on its position [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard voxel grid traversal by using slab-based RLE encoding to skip empty space efficiently [S1, unofficial].
+RLE4 Ray Tracing is a ray-marching and voxel-intersection algorithm that traverses an RLE4 (Run-Length Encoded 4D) compressed volume structure, also known as Map4, to locate the first occupied voxel along a ray or to colorize a voxel based on its position [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard voxel grid traversal by using slab-based RLE encoding to skip empty space efficiently [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Voxel Grid Raycasting](2218-voxel-grid-raycasting.md) by replacing uniform grid stepping with compressed slab lookups.
 
